    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 95,
        "text": "The new shower fittings use less water per minute, but the building total hardly changed.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e04b9784d26300b3ae7c681392275e01a3f7c052b849e8e8522677685558dd90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 102,
        "sourceEnd": 152,
        "text": "Did you compare the same number of occupied rooms?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "08a6e25c27c7a5d75e9dbba0e3a281bbf2e354e1a81da2ed59e40d2003306da1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 159,
        "sourceEnd": 255,
        "text": "No. Occupancy rose from sixty to seventy-two rooms. I compared totals without allowing for that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "2622bf7639c42a0f16144ac9a7c61007ce30181a44850a32dc204168f89b631f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 262,
        "sourceEnd": 338,
        "text": "Calculate consumption per occupied room as well. Did shower duration change?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "b24dc428da5daca67153424880becad333b4781c27732cd47a45dc78922ab1d8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 345,
        "sourceEnd": 504,
        "text": "We have diaries from twelve residents. A few said the warmer spray felt comfortable, so they stayed longer. But diary volunteers may differ from everyone else.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "f655c28473989274fce0f58d28145e3af637390acc39ad22b025211e27ce4584",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 511,
        "sourceEnd": 598,
        "text": "Do not turn twelve diaries into a claim about all residents. What does maintenance say?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "71b5887aaf49709c5b0fd6e7e102bb582ab2e67aa5b11ffbfdb2d0db54d57d89",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 605,
        "sourceEnd": 781,
        "text": "They found a leak in the laundry. It was repaired on the eighteenth, halfway through the observation period. We should show that on the graph rather than draw one smooth trend.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "fa0c0b225406129d43328012d8ac00b5e95de0fad5e1ccfbb06d177b0ee9c052",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 788,
        "sourceEnd": 810,
        "text": "Was the meter checked?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2c9b995cc702a6465346b6912649615c8c84c40d6424d0f20e2a32ca8e23ef91",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 817,
        "sourceEnd": 984,
        "text": "Yes. An engineer compared it with a portable instrument and found no obvious fault. That reduces one possible explanation; it does not prove our preferred explanation.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "0a18fd6fb1d7aed7cc92026edbe1b66908c0a6a65ad25961f3399b17fd344915",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 991,
        "sourceEnd": 1013,
        "text": "What do you recommend?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "b7ae204d28120ba3299d53df6e488afbda969d5bff5baf433355d060d9c5135e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "omar",
        "speaker": "Omar",
        "sourceStart": 1020,
        "sourceEnd": 1185,
        "text": "Keep the fittings and repeat the observation during stable occupancy. Use the same daily recording time, nine in the morning. Report comfort separately from savings.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "2911b7190a2976911babf85fe63a94faf6036ba4afe3994735c025ccbc7eac90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leah",
        "speaker": "Leah",
        "sourceStart": 1192,
        "sourceEnd": 1255,
        "text": "Put the uncertainty in the conclusion, not just in an appendix.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "01c4dcb7a4411b196025983ecccebffaecf414a172418e1e643c45e38761195f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
